WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.635 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Rolling Stone
put out an article.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:05.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was something like
NBA's anti-vaxxer problem,

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.707 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they're pushing around the
league, and all that stuff.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.809
And I had a call
with a journalist,

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.577
and it was all good faith,

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:14.480 align:start position:0%
oh, Jonathan, would love to
get your story, all this stuff,

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.315
and I'm telling him
about why my decision

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:17.650
not to get vaccinated.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.919 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then the article
comes out and it's like,

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.355
Jonathan Isaac waited
for people to die,

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.290
he put his trust in God,
all this different stuff.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.092
I'm like, this is terrible.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.293
And I was furious.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.262 align:start size:88% position:13%
'Cause this is the first
time that I had saw

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:34.334
that there is a
media bias and a,

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
people call it propaganda,
people call it,

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.606
if they want something
to go in a certain way,

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:42.575 align:start size:88% position:13%
they have the power
and the tools to do so,

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.877
and to their discretion.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:46.079
And so that was my first
instance of being like,

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.547
they're right.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.882 align:start size:97% position:3%
People are telling the
truth about all this stuff.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.851
(soft upbeat music)

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.358
- I'm Dave Rubin, we're
here at locals in Miami,

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:01.127 align:start size:97% position:3%
and joining me is a forward
for the Orlando Magic,

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.496 align:start size:81% position:19%
author of the book
"Why I Stand",

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:07.567
and founder of the new
clothing company UNITUS,

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.801
Jonathan Isaac.

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:09.836
Welcome back to
the Rubin Report.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:10.904
- Thank you for having me, man.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.405
Glad to be here.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.606
- I have to say you're the
first person we ever had

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.174 align:start size:88% position:13%
to move a table for,
and actually change some

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:17.644
of the situation that
we have going here.

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:20.346 align:start size:88% position:13%
People wanna know, most
importantly, 6'10"?

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.180
- 6'11".

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.382
- 6'11"!

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:23.583 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Really like seven
something with the hair,

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.452 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I'll be modest.
(Dave laughing)

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.852 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Does the hair
count on rebounding?

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:27.687
- No, it doesn't.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:28.921
- It does not.

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:30.356
It's good to see, again,

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've done a couple
sit-downs over the years,

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.660
obviously NBA player
or author, as I said,

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.395
launching a new brand.

00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:38.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just quick for the people
that don't know you,

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:40.733
gimme a little of the
Jonathan Isaac story,

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.268
getting you to the NBA,

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.104
and then we'll get
into the new stuff.

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.605
- Of getting into the NBA?

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.007 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, give me the life story
that gets you to the NBA,

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.375
and then we'll get
to what you're doing

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.610 align:start size:72% position:28%
these days.
- Super quick.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.145 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like you said, name
Jonathan Isaac.

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:55.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
I grew up in Bronx, New
York, till I was about 10.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.382
Played a little bit
of basketball there,

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.451
but it wasn't my thing.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:59.953
Moved to Naples, Florida,

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:02.288 align:start size:97% position:3%
started to play a little
bit of organized basketball,

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:05.724
fell in love with it, kind
of put everything into it.

00:02:05.724 --> 00:02:08.561 align:start size:97% position:3%
Became the number one player
in the state of Florida.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.062
Went to Florida
State University.

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:12.999
I went to IMG for a year
before that, IMG Academy,

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.500
Florida State University,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.337
and then was drafted six
pick to the Orlando Magic

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.004
back in 2017.

00:02:19.004 --> 00:02:21.173
- And so now you've been
in the NBA, that's what?

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:23.443
Six seasons?
- Six seasons.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:24.543
Couple injuries

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:26.045 align:start size:88% position:13%
along the way.
- Couple injuries, yes.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.179
- But you're healthy now,
you finished the season.

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:28.013
- I'm ready to rock.

00:02:28.013 --> 00:02:29.481
- You're ready to rock.

00:02:29.481 --> 00:02:31.750
So this'll be really your first
season in a couple of years,

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
this upcoming season.
- First full season, yes.

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:37.089
I got to play a little bit
this past season coming back,

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:39.492
it is a big deal when
missing a lot of time,

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.994 align:start size:97% position:3%
but this is my first summer
of being actually able

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:44.497
to work out and not
just be rehabbing.

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.900
It feels good to actually
get in the gym and workout,

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.401
and looking forward to
this upcoming season.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.437 align:start size:97% position:3%
- How does it feel to be
out as long as you were out,

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:54.073 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the ups and downs of
surgery, and all that stuff?

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.176
And you know I have
a torn ACL right now,

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:59.712
so out of four knees here,
you have the two good ones,

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:03.282
ironically, at least
mostly good, I guess.

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:05.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
But just mentally to like
get back on the court

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:06.986 align:start size:84% position:16%
after all that time
and everything.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.388 align:start size:84% position:16%
How does that feel?
- It's tough,

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:10.055
it's tough.

00:03:10.055 --> 00:03:11.324
It's terrible, honestly.

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.360
Going through it,

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.961
it's not just like you
going through an injury

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.096
kind of by yourself.

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.432
You're dealing with it,

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:21.434 align:start size:84% position:16%
you have the fans
are dealing with it,

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.570
the organization
is dealing with it,

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.337 align:start size:88% position:13%
fans, when are you gonna
come back and play?

00:03:25.337 --> 00:03:26.839
Why aren't you playing?

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.841
So it's not something
that's easy to do.

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:31.177
And I know for a fact
that I wouldn't be able

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.679
to kind of press
my way through it

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:34.947
if it wasn't for one, my faith,

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:36.415 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then the people
that I have around me,

00:03:36.415 --> 00:03:39.318
my wife, my family, my
pastor, my church family,

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.621
people to just encourage me
and help me to see the good

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.656
in every single situation
that I'm going through.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:44.958
And that has me here.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:46.525
And also, I think the
last point of that

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:48.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
is just being able to
identify with other people

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:50.562
who get injured now.

00:03:50.562 --> 00:03:55.068
I have a new, I guess
perspective on injury,

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:56.703
and how much grit
and grind it takes,

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:59.138
and how you do get
to see who you are

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:01.107 align:start position:0%
when you're faced with that
kind of adversity as an athlete.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.442
- What about the mental part?

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:03.743
When you get back on the court.

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.411 align:start size:84% position:16%
Your doc says, okay,
your knee's fine,

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.413 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you're like,
your body feels good,

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:09.215
'cause I can tell you
that I'm no NBA player,

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:11.450 align:start size:84% position:16%
but just from playing
with a weak knee,

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.352 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's more mental that
I'm always worried about

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:14.520
when I'm running
around out there

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.089
than the physical part in a way.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.390
- Honestly, it's
like riding a bike.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:21.694 align:start size:97% position:3%
I have heard that it's
very tough for certain guys

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.030
when you get back just
kind of trusting it.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.297
For me, that really wasn't

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:26.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
my issue.
- You just trust the doc.

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:27.333
- Well, not the doc.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.468
I just trust that
I'm ready to go.

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:31.003
My trust is in God,
and so I'm just like,

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:33.873 align:start size:97% position:3%
look, I'm healed, they say I'm
cleared, I'm ready to rock.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.142
And I just kind of put one
foot in front of the other.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:39.545 align:start size:84% position:16%
And once you get
the training wheels,

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.780
once you get like,

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.481
okay, I jumped, I fell,
and nothing happened,

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:43.716
you kind of just
forget about it.

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:45.418 align:start size:81% position:19%
But I do know that
for some people

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.487
it is very difficult to
get back on the court

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.155
after a big injury like that.

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:51.156 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So the thing that kind
of put you on the map

00:04:51.156 --> 00:04:55.528 align:start size:97% position:3%
during Covid and all of
the BLM stuff and all that,

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:58.130
you stood for the
national anthem,

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.699
which was not that
popular at the time.

00:05:00.699 --> 00:05:01.634 align:start size:84% position:16%
- At all.
(Jonathan laughing)

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:02.568
- When you look back on that,

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.036
do you think it was like,

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:06.505
well, I have no doubt that
you're proud of what you did,

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:09.008
but does it seem like a crazy
time to look back on that?

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:10.710
The bubble with the NBA?

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.411
Just the whole situation.

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:13.313
- Insane.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:17.183
It's weird 'cause now like
kind of the dust has settled,

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.786
things have come out about
BLM and the organization,

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:22.488
the way that they handle
funds, and stuff like that.

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:26.792
So it's just like, it's not
as kind of potent right now,

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:29.328
but when you go back in
time, even Covid stuff,

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:31.764 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's died down, people
aren't as emotional about it,

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:35.935
but in the heat of it,
it was like Armageddon.

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:38.137
It was real.

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:41.841 align:start position:0%
So to be in that moment of
deciding on what I was gonna do,

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:44.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
how I was gonna handle the
pressure of the moment,

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:48.580 align:start size:88% position:13%
it really was, it
really, really, really,
really was tough.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.215
- So then you do that,

00:05:50.215 --> 00:05:53.452 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then kind of you
get welcomed by a
whole bunch of people

00:05:53.452 --> 00:05:55.922
that maybe politically
you probably thought

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:57.556
maybe either weren't your people

00:05:57.556 --> 00:05:59.358
or it was just like a
community of people,

00:05:59.358 --> 00:06:01.660 align:start size:97% position:3%
you published your book
with The Daily Wire, right?

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:03.529 align:start size:97% position:3%
These were probably not
things you would've expected.

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.897
Can you talk about what
it was like to kind of

00:06:05.897 --> 00:06:07.699 align:start size:84% position:16%
go in that direction,
so to speak?

00:06:07.699 --> 00:06:12.271
- Yeah, I mean, so after I
decided to stand in a bubble,

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:14.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
and go through that entire
process, that was a-

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:16.609
- Were were you literally
the only player that did?

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:18.077
- No, one other player did.

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:20.513
I believe Meyers Leonard.

00:06:20.513 --> 00:06:21.848 align:start size:81% position:19%
He did, I believe-
- Oh, he's not

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:23.015
even in the league anymore,

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:23.549 align:start size:97% position:3%
right?
- No, he's not in the league

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:25.084
anymore.

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:26.618
- That's interesting, there
was some other stuff there,

00:06:26.618 --> 00:06:28.220
but he's young enough and
skilled enough to still be

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.088 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the league.
- No, I'm pretty sure

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:30.323
he can definitely play.

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:35.461
But yeah, so there was a ton
of negativity around the stand.

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:38.998
Obviously people were upset
about me deciding to stand,

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:40.465
and not kneel.

00:06:40.465 --> 00:06:44.102
But then you talked about there
was an overwhelming support,

00:06:44.102 --> 00:06:46.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
obviously, of Christians,
people who understood

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:49.541
the heartbeat of why I decided
to stand in the first place.

00:06:49.541 --> 00:06:52.044 align:start size:88% position:13%
I never felt comfortable
with the tone

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:53.946
and the rhetoric of the Black
Lives Matter organization,

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:56.649
and I didn't want to
co-sign their message

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:58.651
by putting on their t-shirt.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:01.153
And also I didn't wanna
co-sign their message

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:02.621
by kneeling.

00:07:02.621 --> 00:07:05.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so there was that
kind of conservative folks

00:07:05.357 --> 00:07:08.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
that obviously see this
kind of person standing up

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:10.996
for the flag, and they
kind of latched onto it.

00:07:10.996 --> 00:07:13.999 align:start size:97% position:3%
But I tried my best to
stay true to my message of,

00:07:13.999 --> 00:07:16.902 align:start size:97% position:3%
I believe that if we decide
all of us white, Black,

00:07:16.902 --> 00:07:18.270
and different choose
to love each other,

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:21.240
like God loves us, which
is in spite of our sin,

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.775
instead of our shortcomings,

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:24.910
and realizing that we all
fall short of God's glory,

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.246
we could have real
progress and change.

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:28.681
And so that's what I stuck to,

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:33.319 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I wasn't negative towards
that kind of attention.

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:35.855 align:start size:88% position:13%
They definitely welcomed
me with open arms,

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:37.089
and being able to publish
a book with The Daily Wire,

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:38.558
I started to learn
about these people,

00:07:38.558 --> 00:07:41.627 align:start size:88% position:13%
and they showed me love,
they showed me love.

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:43.262 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So they're not a
bunch of crazy racists?

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:46.064
- No, that's not
what I got from,

00:07:46.064 --> 00:07:49.768 align:start position:0%
I would get questions about
why would you publish your book

00:07:49.768 --> 00:07:50.769
with The Daily Wire?

00:07:50.769 --> 00:07:52.237
They're all racist.

00:07:52.237 --> 00:07:55.073 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I'm like, well, why
would they publish my book?

00:07:55.073 --> 00:07:59.378
Obviously there is an
ideological similarity

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:03.482 align:start size:84% position:16%
that trumps skin
color in their eyes,

00:08:03.482 --> 00:08:04.650
or they wouldn't
publish my book.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:05.852
It would be like,

00:08:05.852 --> 00:08:06.786 align:start size:88% position:13%
okay, we might agree
with him on some things,

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:08.687
but he's Black, not gonna do it.

00:08:08.687 --> 00:08:10.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
So obviously that trumped
the color of my skin.

00:08:10.989 --> 00:08:13.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
And even with Ben Shapiro
being an Orthodox Jew

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:16.695 align:start size:97% position:3%
and me being a Christian still
decided to publish my book.

00:08:16.695 --> 00:08:18.865
And my book is like all about
Jesus at the end of the day.

00:08:18.865 --> 00:08:20.766 align:start size:81% position:19%
- And you're 6'11"
and he's 4'2",

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:22.268
so there's a huge discrepancy.

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:23.269
- Yeah, very intimidating.

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:24.170
(Dave laughing)

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.604
And so, yeah.

00:08:25.604 --> 00:08:29.341 align:start size:97% position:3%
So no, it was a great process,
very tough, like I said.

00:08:29.341 --> 00:08:30.843
There was one moment,

00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:33.345 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I tried my best to spell
this all out in the book,

00:08:33.345 --> 00:08:35.481
but I was on the phone
with my pastor the night

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:38.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
before I decided to stand,
and I'm telling him,

00:08:38.617 --> 00:08:40.987
I don't think you understand
how crazy this is gonna be.

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:42.421
I hadn't signed my contract yet,

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:45.024 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was up for an
extension that summer,

00:08:45.024 --> 00:08:46.358 align:start size:81% position:19%
I knew I was gonna
be name called,

00:08:46.358 --> 00:08:48.127
I knew I was gonna
be ridiculed for it.

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:49.628
And he said to me,

00:08:49.628 --> 00:08:51.564
you cannot stand for God
and God not stand for you.

00:08:51.564 --> 00:08:53.466
And so that was kind
of the mic drop moment.

00:08:53.466 --> 00:08:55.501 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was like, all
right, I'm doing it.

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:57.536
And we went full speed ahead.

00:08:57.536 --> 00:09:00.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, and it's basically
worked since then.

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:02.141
You're doing a lot of stuff,

00:09:02.141 --> 00:09:03.943
including you got a
new three-month old
in your life too.

00:09:03.943 --> 00:09:05.945
- Yes, even talking
about doing stuff,

00:09:05.945 --> 00:09:07.613
I never in a million
years would've thought

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:08.814
that I'd be an author.

00:09:08.814 --> 00:09:10.349
So even when I get
introduced like that,

00:09:10.349 --> 00:09:11.951
Jonathan Isaac, the
author, NBA player,

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:13.152
I'm like, what?

00:09:13.152 --> 00:09:14.520
That still doesn't
make any sense to me.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.355
But to be an author,
to have that come out

00:09:16.355 --> 00:09:19.792 align:start size:97% position:3%
of this moment of standing,
it is really surreal.

00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:21.526
And now I got a baby girl,

00:09:21.526 --> 00:09:22.661
three months old.
- How's fatherhood

00:09:22.661 --> 00:09:23.529
treating you?

00:09:23.529 --> 00:09:24.363
(Jonathan sighing)

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:25.698
- I love it.

00:09:25.698 --> 00:09:26.932
There's not many words for it,

00:09:26.932 --> 00:09:29.401
or to try to put it into
its right perspective,

00:09:29.401 --> 00:09:32.104 align:start size:97% position:3%
but it is that unconditional
love for something

00:09:32.104 --> 00:09:34.407 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you know you're
responsible for.

00:09:34.407 --> 00:09:36.976
And so it's been amazing.

00:09:36.976 --> 00:09:39.845
- Yeah, so all of
this stuff happens,

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:41.213
you get some of the pushback,

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:43.315
now seeing some of
the dust settle,

00:09:43.315 --> 00:09:45.418
the guys come up to you
now, and they're like,

00:09:45.418 --> 00:09:47.053 align:start size:84% position:16%
hey, maybe I should
have done that,

00:09:47.053 --> 00:09:48.721
or I respect what you did,

00:09:48.721 --> 00:09:49.855
is there any of that kind stuff?

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:51.023
Or is everyone?

00:09:51.023 --> 00:09:54.093 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah, I've had plenty
of conversations,

00:09:54.093 --> 00:09:55.594
not just for the BLM stuff,

00:09:55.594 --> 00:09:57.763
but I would say even more
so for the Covid stuff.

00:09:57.763 --> 00:09:59.031
- Right, that was the next-

00:09:59.031 --> 00:10:00.533
- So it is something
that people forget,

00:10:00.533 --> 00:10:02.535
but even that moment was like,

00:10:02.535 --> 00:10:03.969
I'm the only player on my team,

00:10:03.969 --> 00:10:06.705
and one of a handful
of guys in the NBA

00:10:06.705 --> 00:10:08.574
that decided not
to get vaccinated.

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:09.775
And so that was-

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:11.477 align:start size:88% position:13%
- We'll throw to a video
of that right here,

00:10:11.477 --> 00:10:13.646
so that people can see it again.

00:10:13.646 --> 00:10:16.848 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I'm not anti-vax,
I'm not anti-medicine,

00:10:16.848 --> 00:10:18.851
I'm not anti-science,

00:10:18.851 --> 00:10:21.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't come to my
current vaccination status

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:22.955
by studying Black history,

00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:25.290 align:start size:88% position:13%
or watching Donald
Trump press conferences.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:27.025
I have nothing but
the utmost respect

00:10:27.025 --> 00:10:30.962 align:start size:97% position:3%
for every healthcare worker
and person in Orlando,

00:10:30.962 --> 00:10:33.499
and all across the world
that have worked tirelessly

00:10:33.499 --> 00:10:35.001
to keep us safe.

00:10:35.001 --> 00:10:37.970 align:start position:0%
My mom has worked in healthcare
for a really long time.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:40.640
I thank God, I'm grateful
that I live in a society

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:44.977
where vaccines are possible,
and we can protect ourselves,

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:46.379
and have the means
to protect ourselves

00:10:46.379 --> 00:10:48.414
in the first place.

00:10:48.414 --> 00:10:50.483
But with that being
said, it is my belief

00:10:50.483 --> 00:10:53.619 align:start size:84% position:16%
that the vaccine
status of every person

00:10:53.619 --> 00:10:56.188
should be their own choice,

00:10:56.188 --> 00:10:59.125
and completely up to
them without bullying,

00:10:59.125 --> 00:11:00.326
without being pressured,

00:11:00.326 --> 00:11:01.893 align:start size:84% position:16%
or without being
forced into doing so.

00:11:01.893 --> 00:11:04.730
I'm not ashamed to say
that I'm uncomfortable

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:07.266 align:start size:84% position:16%
with taking the
vaccine at this time.

00:11:07.266 --> 00:11:08.701 align:start size:81% position:19%
I think that we're
all different.

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:09.935
We all come from
different places.

00:11:09.935 --> 00:11:11.537
We've all have had
different experiences

00:11:11.537 --> 00:11:13.439
and hold dear to
different beliefs.

00:11:13.439 --> 00:11:15.574
And what it is that
you do with your body

00:11:15.574 --> 00:11:17.876 align:start size:88% position:13%
when it comes to putting
medicine in there

00:11:17.876 --> 00:11:20.880
should be your choice
free of the ridicule

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:22.381
and the opinion of others.

00:11:22.381 --> 00:11:24.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
- But was that completely
on the fly for you?

00:11:24.616 --> 00:11:27.586
I mean, I guess everyone
was being asked questions

00:11:27.586 --> 00:11:29.989
like that, but were you
planning on that moment?

00:11:29.989 --> 00:11:31.857
- So this is what happened.

00:11:31.857 --> 00:11:33.925 align:start size:88% position:13%
What happened was not
to take up too much time

00:11:33.925 --> 00:11:36.662
on this topic, but
what happened was,

00:11:36.662 --> 00:11:37.863
I had gone through
the whole thing,

00:11:37.863 --> 00:11:39.131
I saw everything
that was going out.

00:11:39.131 --> 00:11:41.767
People were being
crazy about Covid,

00:11:41.767 --> 00:11:44.236
all these weird things about
why you should get a shot,

00:11:44.236 --> 00:11:46.372
and incentivizing
you to get a shot.

00:11:46.372 --> 00:11:47.673 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then obviously
you're getting bullied

00:11:47.673 --> 00:11:49.108
if you even have any
questions about it,

00:11:49.108 --> 00:11:50.409
natural immunity,
all that stuff.

00:11:50.409 --> 00:11:51.911
- You didn't wanna do it
for the free hamburger?

00:11:51.911 --> 00:11:55.114
- I'm like, if you're trying
to get somebody to do something

00:11:55.114 --> 00:11:57.249
threatening them is only
gonna make them more weary.

00:11:57.249 --> 00:11:58.350 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm like, I don't
know what's going on,

00:11:58.350 --> 00:11:59.752
but I decided not to do it.

00:12:00.853 --> 00:12:03.955 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then Rolling Stone
put out an article,

00:12:03.955 --> 00:12:07.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was something like
NBA's anti-vaxxer problem,

00:12:07.059 --> 00:12:08.994 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they're pushing around the
league, and all that stuff.

00:12:08.994 --> 00:12:11.096
And I had a call
with a journalist,

00:12:11.096 --> 00:12:12.864
and it was all good faith,

00:12:12.864 --> 00:12:15.801 align:start position:0%
oh, Jonathan, would love to
get your story, all this stuff.

00:12:15.801 --> 00:12:17.636
And I'm telling him
about why my decision

00:12:17.636 --> 00:12:19.071
not to get vaccinated.

00:12:19.071 --> 00:12:21.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the article
comes out, and it's like,

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:23.675
Jonathan Isaac waited
for people to die,

00:12:23.675 --> 00:12:25.611
he put his trust in God,
all this different stuff.

00:12:25.611 --> 00:12:27.479
I'm like, this is terrible.

00:12:27.479 --> 00:12:28.681
And I was furious.

00:12:28.681 --> 00:12:30.549 align:start size:88% position:13%
'Cause this is the first
time that I had saw

00:12:30.549 --> 00:12:34.019
that there is a media bias,

00:12:34.019 --> 00:12:37.389 align:start size:97% position:3%
and people call it
propaganda, people call it,

00:12:38.557 --> 00:12:40.793
if they want something
to go in a certain way,

00:12:40.793 --> 00:12:43.762 align:start size:88% position:13%
they have the power
and the tools to do so,

00:12:43.762 --> 00:12:45.030
and to their discretion.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:47.265
And so that was my first
instance of being like,

00:12:47.265 --> 00:12:49.401
they're right, people
are telling the truth

00:12:49.401 --> 00:12:50.970
about all this stuff, and so-

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.638 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Once you see that,
isn't it freaky?

00:12:52.638 --> 00:12:53.906
- Yes.

00:12:53.906 --> 00:12:55.441 align:start size:81% position:19%
- 'Cause no matter
how you see it,

00:12:55.441 --> 00:12:56.675
no matter what leads you to
that moment of seeing it,

00:12:56.675 --> 00:12:57.977
once you see it,
you can't unsee it.

00:12:57.977 --> 00:12:59.512
- It's freaky, but
it's freeing too.

00:12:59.512 --> 00:13:00.679
'Cause now I'm like, okay.

00:13:00.679 --> 00:13:02.748
It's like, I had my moment of,

00:13:02.748 --> 00:13:04.950
okay, I know what
all this means.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.285
And so I was preparing myself

00:13:07.285 --> 00:13:09.488 align:start size:97% position:3%
because I had media day coming
up literally the next day

00:13:09.488 --> 00:13:10.790
after the article dropped.

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:12.524 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I knew I was
gonna get questions.

00:13:12.524 --> 00:13:14.627 align:start position:0%
People were tweeting me,
telling me I'm crazy and stupid,

00:13:14.627 --> 00:13:16.495 align:start size:88% position:13%
and all this stuff,
and I'm an anti-vaxxer.

00:13:16.495 --> 00:13:19.030
And so I took that kind
of that night to be like,

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:21.233
okay, I know what it
is that I stand for,

00:13:21.233 --> 00:13:22.734
I know why I did what I did,

00:13:22.734 --> 00:13:24.503
and now taking it and kind
of just prepared myself,

00:13:24.503 --> 00:13:26.171
and then I got the questions.

00:13:26.171 --> 00:13:30.542
- Yeah, so the Covid
thing, the BLM thing,

00:13:30.542 --> 00:13:34.914
the injury thing, all of
this stuff, fatherhood,

00:13:34.914 --> 00:13:35.948
then you get back on the court

00:13:35.948 --> 00:13:37.482
just for the end of the season.

00:13:37.482 --> 00:13:40.352
I mean, that's like a lot of
stuff that that you kind of,

00:13:40.352 --> 00:13:41.820
oh, you release a book.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:45.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, and it's speaking
gigs, all that stuff,

00:13:45.391 --> 00:13:47.960 align:start size:84% position:16%
just to get you to
just to what you love,

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:49.961
and what your main gig is.

00:13:49.961 --> 00:13:50.896
It's pretty amazing.

00:13:50.896 --> 00:13:52.430
- I mean, I just stayed busy.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.634
I was rehabbing every day,
I was putting in the work,

00:13:55.634 --> 00:13:58.337
but I had free time
on my hands to do,

00:13:58.337 --> 00:14:00.205
and to think and create,

00:14:00.205 --> 00:14:03.808
and just try my best to be an
inspiration to other people

00:14:03.808 --> 00:14:05.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
who also found themselves
in this moment,

00:14:05.711 --> 00:14:09.381 align:start size:84% position:16%
but didn't have either
the courage or the
people around them

00:14:09.381 --> 00:14:11.917 align:start size:97% position:3%
to stand, and that's something
that it wasn't all me.

00:14:11.917 --> 00:14:14.920
I had people around me
pushing me to be a light

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:17.289 align:start size:97% position:3%
to other people, and so
that's why a lot of the stuff

00:14:17.289 --> 00:14:18.556
that I did, I decided to do it.

00:14:18.556 --> 00:14:19.758
- Do you think you
were proven right,

00:14:19.758 --> 00:14:21.226
not only on the Covid stuff,

00:14:21.226 --> 00:14:23.195
but even on a lot
of the woke stuff?

00:14:23.195 --> 00:14:26.297
And then this will sort of
get us to UNITUS in a sec.

00:14:26.297 --> 00:14:29.568 align:start size:97% position:3%
But the NBA even has scaled
back on the woke stuff,

00:14:29.568 --> 00:14:32.404
they had the BLM
logos on the court,

00:14:32.404 --> 00:14:34.006
basically those are gone.

00:14:34.006 --> 00:14:36.475 align:start size:84% position:16%
They seem like they've
shifted out of it.

00:14:36.475 --> 00:14:37.742
The NHL, for example,

00:14:37.742 --> 00:14:39.978
they're not gonna do
Pride night anymore.

00:14:39.978 --> 00:14:42.314
Just these things that
they push on everybody,

00:14:42.314 --> 00:14:44.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
it does seem like there's
been some reversal

00:14:44.416 --> 00:14:45.517 align:start size:81% position:19%
with some of that.
- Yeah, 1,000%.

00:14:45.517 --> 00:14:47.352
A 1,000% there is,

00:14:47.352 --> 00:14:51.189
I think that it's just when
you get to these moments

00:14:51.189 --> 00:14:54.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
of hostility and
everything is at the rise,

00:14:54.593 --> 00:14:56.929
it is very easy to jump on,

00:14:56.929 --> 00:14:58.664
we wanna support this,
and we wanna push this.

00:14:58.664 --> 00:15:00.299
But when the dust does settle,

00:15:00.299 --> 00:15:02.468
and kind of everybody kind of
comes back to their senses,

00:15:02.468 --> 00:15:03.602
and okay, what is going on?

00:15:03.602 --> 00:15:05.103
Where are things at?

00:15:05.103 --> 00:15:08.106
I do think the kind of
rational thing to do is

00:15:08.106 --> 00:15:13.078 align:start size:97% position:3%
to scale back and kind of
get back to program as usual.

00:15:13.078 --> 00:15:15.113 align:start position:0%
And that's what a lot of
people and companies have done.

00:15:15.113 --> 00:15:16.949
- I'm guessing most of
the players probably feel

00:15:16.949 --> 00:15:18.516
that way too privately, right?

00:15:18.516 --> 00:15:20.585
That they're just like,
I just wanna play ball,

00:15:20.585 --> 00:15:21.620
more than anything else.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.022
- I think even past players,

00:15:23.022 --> 00:15:25.958 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think that's just
most Americans,

00:15:27.326 --> 00:15:28.827
especially when it comes to
sports and entertainment,

00:15:28.827 --> 00:15:30.829
they do just want to enjoy.

00:15:30.829 --> 00:15:35.534
And I'm not saying that the
free choice for companies

00:15:35.534 --> 00:15:37.736
to voice their opinion on issues

00:15:37.736 --> 00:15:41.039 align:start size:88% position:13%
that they feel strongly
about is wrong,

00:15:41.039 --> 00:15:42.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that that's the
great thing about America,

00:15:42.608 --> 00:15:44.343
people are free to do so,

00:15:44.343 --> 00:15:47.379
but I do think that in
sport and entertainment,

00:15:47.379 --> 00:15:50.815
there should be discretion
and there should be nuance

00:15:50.815 --> 00:15:53.051 align:start size:97% position:3%
that the people that are
watching are not all the same,

00:15:53.051 --> 00:15:54.853 align:start size:84% position:16%
they don't all believe
the same things,

00:15:54.853 --> 00:15:58.090
and that should go
into your messaging

00:15:58.090 --> 00:15:59.791
and what you decide
to put out there.

00:15:59.791 --> 00:16:01.893
And not demonizing one set
of people, or one group,

00:16:01.893 --> 00:16:06.098
or one side, but just trying
to share your view as a company

00:16:06.098 --> 00:16:07.166
and as a person.

00:16:07.166 --> 00:16:08.533
And I think at the same time,

00:16:08.533 --> 00:16:10.435 align:start size:84% position:16%
if the league is
comfortable doing it,

00:16:10.435 --> 00:16:12.905
they should then be
just as comfortable

00:16:12.905 --> 00:16:14.505 align:start size:84% position:16%
allowing their
athletes to do it too,

00:16:14.505 --> 00:16:16.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
even if it's in a way that
they don't agree with.

00:16:16.541 --> 00:16:18.944
- Right, that seems to be
the part that the leagues

00:16:18.944 --> 00:16:20.346
never get on board with, right?

00:16:20.346 --> 00:16:22.481 align:start size:84% position:16%
The two-way street
portion of this thing.

00:16:23.849 --> 00:16:27.385
So you mentioned Naples,
now you play for Orlando,

00:16:27.385 --> 00:16:30.556 align:start size:84% position:16%
Florida guy,
according to the media

00:16:30.556 --> 00:16:32.190
that you no longer trust,

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:34.526
I thought Florida's no
good for Black people.

00:16:34.526 --> 00:16:36.395 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Stop it.
(both laughing)

00:16:36.395 --> 00:16:37.629
- Isn't that what they tell us?

00:16:37.629 --> 00:16:40.565
- I mean, I've been okay
here for a while, and-

00:16:40.565 --> 00:16:43.201
- And you're not hiding,
you're not hiding at 6'11".

00:16:43.201 --> 00:16:44.136
- Yeah, no, I mean,

00:16:44.136 --> 00:16:47.272
look, no place is perfect.

00:16:48.373 --> 00:16:49.975
Every place has their
ups and their downs,

00:16:49.975 --> 00:16:53.345
but to espouse that Black
people can't be in Florida,

00:16:53.345 --> 00:16:54.980
it is ridiculous.

00:16:56.348 --> 00:16:59.084
And that's that kind of the
nuance that people don't,

00:16:59.084 --> 00:17:00.786
everything is just so
polarizing these days,

00:17:00.786 --> 00:17:03.722
you get the hits and you get
the controversy and the likes

00:17:03.722 --> 00:17:05.591 align:start size:88% position:13%
by saying something
extremely controversial,

00:17:05.591 --> 00:17:07.025
and then it goes everywhere.

00:17:07.025 --> 00:17:08.227
One side is saying,

00:17:08.227 --> 00:17:09.728 align:start size:84% position:16%
oh, I can't believe
they said that.

00:17:09.728 --> 00:17:11.797
And the other side is trying
to back what the person said,

00:17:11.797 --> 00:17:13.231
but obviously that's false

00:17:13.231 --> 00:17:16.268 align:start position:0%
with the amount of African
Americans that live in Florida.

00:17:16.268 --> 00:17:17.569
- You know what the
number one state

00:17:17.569 --> 00:17:19.705
for Black-owned
small businesses?

00:17:19.705 --> 00:17:21.173
- Is it Florida?

00:17:21.173 --> 00:17:22.107
There you go.

00:17:22.107 --> 00:17:23.374
- It is Florida, there you go.

00:17:23.374 --> 00:17:25.744
So speaking of business,
you're starting UNITUS,

00:17:25.744 --> 00:17:28.513
which now is going
to be basically,

00:17:28.513 --> 00:17:30.582 align:start size:97% position:3%
well, you tell me, I don't
wanna put words in your mouth.

00:17:30.582 --> 00:17:31.583
I was gonna say something.

00:17:31.583 --> 00:17:32.751
You tell me what it's gonna be.

00:17:32.751 --> 00:17:34.619
- So back in 2020,

00:17:34.619 --> 00:17:36.822 align:start size:97% position:3%
same kind of around that time
of the BLM and the Covid,

00:17:36.822 --> 00:17:38.390
I was a Nike-signed athlete,

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:40.826
and paid by Nike,
signed by Nike.

00:17:40.826 --> 00:17:42.394 align:start size:84% position:16%
And after I got
injured, I ended up-

00:17:42.394 --> 00:17:43.661 align:start size:84% position:16%
- How does that
process go by the way,

00:17:43.661 --> 00:17:46.231
when you're drafted,
they're bringing in,

00:17:46.231 --> 00:17:47.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
do all the shoe
companies come up to you,

00:17:47.833 --> 00:17:49.934
and everybody's trying to
figure out who to go to?

00:17:49.934 --> 00:17:51.136
Are you going to them?

00:17:51.136 --> 00:17:54.206 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It depends largely
on who you wore

00:17:54.206 --> 00:17:55.473
as a college athlete as well.

00:17:55.473 --> 00:17:58.377
And so I've worn Nike
kind of my whole life

00:17:58.377 --> 00:17:59.411
once I got into basketball,

00:17:59.411 --> 00:18:00.979
so I was in the EYBL,

00:18:00.979 --> 00:18:03.949
which is Nike's kind
of youth AAU circuit.

00:18:03.949 --> 00:18:06.718
So I was always wearing
Nike then, loved it.

00:18:07.719 --> 00:18:09.187
When I got to Florida State,

00:18:09.187 --> 00:18:12.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
Florida State's a Nike
school, got to the league.

00:18:12.791 --> 00:18:14.626 align:start size:88% position:13%
Well, when transitioning
into the league,

00:18:14.626 --> 00:18:17.896
I was courted by Adidas for a
while, but no other companies.

00:18:17.896 --> 00:18:20.532 align:start size:97% position:3%
I was kind of adamant about
I wanna be a Nike guy.

00:18:20.532 --> 00:18:22.167
And ended up signing with them.

00:18:22.167 --> 00:18:23.701
And it was great.

00:18:23.701 --> 00:18:27.138
Like I love Nike, and I have
loved Nike for a long time,

00:18:27.138 --> 00:18:31.143
I disagree with them and
a lot of other companies

00:18:31.143 --> 00:18:32.610
have kind of made
conscious decisions

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:36.415
over the last few years to
move in a specific direction,

00:18:36.415 --> 00:18:39.184 align:start size:88% position:13%
this is what they're
saying that they're for.

00:18:39.184 --> 00:18:40.651
And when it comes to UNITUS,

00:18:40.651 --> 00:18:42.921
for me it's just about
freedom, it's just about,

00:18:42.921 --> 00:18:44.556
look, these companies
are allowed to do it,

00:18:44.556 --> 00:18:47.092
just like I talked about the
organizations like the NBA,

00:18:47.092 --> 00:18:49.894 align:start size:97% position:3%
but we're also free to
support what we wanna support.

00:18:49.894 --> 00:18:53.932 align:start position:0%
And if I could create something
that stands up for family,

00:18:53.932 --> 00:18:56.735
faith, freedom, and
the values and ideals

00:18:56.735 --> 00:18:59.137
that one has made
this country great,

00:18:59.137 --> 00:19:01.773
has made this country prosper,

00:19:01.773 --> 00:19:05.844
and have the progress that
it has had from its founding,

00:19:05.844 --> 00:19:09.114
and then just stay true to
who I am as a Christian man,

00:19:09.114 --> 00:19:11.282
and athlete, and person.

00:19:11.282 --> 00:19:13.685 align:start size:97% position:3%
I want those values to be
celebrated in the marketplace

00:19:13.685 --> 00:19:16.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
and in the culture, and
what better way to do that

00:19:16.655 --> 00:19:18.857 align:start size:88% position:13%
than through really
cool, awesome clothing?

00:19:18.857 --> 00:19:21.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, so it's an
athletic wear brand that-

00:19:21.393 --> 00:19:22.927
- Athletic wear
and leisure wear.

00:19:22.927 --> 00:19:24.596
- [Dave] And leisure wear,
so we'll show some images

00:19:24.596 --> 00:19:26.164
while we're talking right now.

00:19:26.164 --> 00:19:28.299
How does this even begin?

00:19:28.299 --> 00:19:29.400
How does this happen?

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:30.902 align:start size:88% position:13%
That one day-
- Yeah, great question.

00:19:30.902 --> 00:19:32.404
- [Dave] Did you have the idea
and then you go to somebody?

00:19:32.404 --> 00:19:33.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did somebody come to you?
- No, no no.

00:19:33.838 --> 00:19:36.909 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'll tell you, so my pastor's
a huge part of my life.

00:19:38.243 --> 00:19:39.710
Like I told you, I was
on the phone with him

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:41.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
the night before I decided
to stand in a bubble.

00:19:41.679 --> 00:19:44.249
But just talking to him,

00:19:44.249 --> 00:19:46.418
and he was the reason why
I wrote the book as well.

00:19:46.418 --> 00:19:49.287
He comes rushing over to
my house one day and says,

00:19:49.287 --> 00:19:52.457
people know your stand, but
they don't know your story.

00:19:52.457 --> 00:19:54.192
And that was the
thing of saying,

00:19:54.192 --> 00:19:56.361
you need to write a book,
and you need to do a movie,

00:19:56.361 --> 00:19:58.129
all this different stuff.

00:19:58.129 --> 00:19:59.331
- Is the movie coming?

00:19:59.331 --> 00:20:01.600
- We've been in talks
for quite a while.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:03.568
But if anybody wants to do
the "Why I Stand" movie,

00:20:03.568 --> 00:20:04.403
hit me up.

00:20:04.403 --> 00:20:05.870
- All right.

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:10.175
- But yeah, so after I
didn't re-sign with Nike,

00:20:10.175 --> 00:20:11.476
talking to him, he says,

00:20:11.476 --> 00:20:14.012
you should look into
creating your own shoe,

00:20:14.012 --> 00:20:16.148 align:start size:84% position:16%
something that stands
for your values,

00:20:16.148 --> 00:20:17.950
and that you can use for you.

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:19.117
It wasn't necessarily something

00:20:19.117 --> 00:20:21.286 align:start size:88% position:13%
that could be broadcast
this to everybody,

00:20:21.286 --> 00:20:23.655
and I said, I don't
think you understand

00:20:23.655 --> 00:20:25.089
how hard it is to create a shoe.

00:20:25.089 --> 00:20:26.458
This isn't easy.
(Dave laughing)

00:20:26.458 --> 00:20:28.159
And I've learned
how difficult it is

00:20:28.159 --> 00:20:32.130
to create a high-value,
high-performance shoe.

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:34.065 align:start size:84% position:16%
But to his guidance,
I kind of said,

00:20:34.065 --> 00:20:36.201
I'll set out and see
what it looks like,

00:20:36.201 --> 00:20:40.472 align:start position:0%
had some conversations, and
then was like, I'm gonna do it.

00:20:40.472 --> 00:20:44.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that vision of just
creating a shoe for myself

00:20:44.076 --> 00:20:46.678
to wear during the
season turned into,

00:20:46.678 --> 00:20:49.982 align:start size:97% position:3%
there are so many people
that believe like I believe,

00:20:49.982 --> 00:20:53.318
and as I see the decline
of these values and ideals

00:20:53.318 --> 00:20:54.987 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I believe deserve
to be celebrated

00:20:54.987 --> 00:20:57.656 align:start size:97% position:3%
as I see their decline in
the marketplace and culture,

00:20:59.057 --> 00:21:01.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
why not give these people
something for them?

00:21:01.793 --> 00:21:03.828
Give them a home, build
a community of people

00:21:03.828 --> 00:21:06.732
that are saying, we
love these values,

00:21:06.732 --> 00:21:07.899
and we stand on these values.

00:21:07.899 --> 00:21:11.136 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I think with
being the only person

00:21:11.136 --> 00:21:12.637
to do a couple of things,

00:21:12.637 --> 00:21:15.740
I do know how lonely it is
to do something by yourself.

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:19.277 align:start position:0%
And I know that the fear aspect
and the intimidation aspect

00:21:19.277 --> 00:21:22.480
of everything that's going on
around you is very daunting.

00:21:22.480 --> 00:21:25.951 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so if I can help people
have a sense of pride

00:21:25.951 --> 00:21:27.586
about their values and ideals,

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:30.321
and be able to wear
it on their sleeve,

00:21:30.321 --> 00:21:31.856 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think that's something
that's beautiful,

00:21:31.856 --> 00:21:34.393
and American, and free.

00:21:34.393 --> 00:21:36.561
And so that vision started

00:21:36.561 --> 00:21:37.896
to kind of bounce
around in my head,

00:21:37.896 --> 00:21:41.133
and he came up with
the name UNITUS,

00:21:41.133 --> 00:21:43.702
and we were just kind
of playing with it,

00:21:43.702 --> 00:21:46.171
and from there I've
just been kind of

00:21:46.171 --> 00:21:48.674
executing in the background,
not saying anything to anybody.

00:21:48.674 --> 00:21:50.042
- So what do you do?

00:21:50.042 --> 00:21:51.243
Was the first idea,

00:21:51.243 --> 00:21:52.477 align:start size:84% position:16%
okay, I'm gonna
create the shoe first?

00:21:52.477 --> 00:21:54.012
- Yeah, the shoe started first.

00:21:54.012 --> 00:21:57.182 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I am gonna be debuting a
shoe at some point this summer

00:21:57.182 --> 00:21:58.917
that I will be wearing
this upcoming season.

00:21:58.917 --> 00:22:00.085
It's called the Judah One,

00:22:00.085 --> 00:22:01.419
gonna be five colorways,

00:22:01.419 --> 00:22:03.254
each colorway has
a different verse,

00:22:03.254 --> 00:22:06.057
Bible verse that goes with
the colorway and the shoe.

00:22:06.057 --> 00:22:09.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that's not necessarily
UNITUS just yet.

00:22:09.394 --> 00:22:11.096
One of the things about
UNITUS is I wanna be able

00:22:11.096 --> 00:22:14.399 align:start size:97% position:3%
to sign athletes from all
different sports as we grow,

00:22:15.466 --> 00:22:17.702 align:start size:84% position:16%
value aligned athletes
to be ambassadors

00:22:17.702 --> 00:22:19.737
and forward runners for
the company and brand.

00:22:19.737 --> 00:22:21.539 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm gonna be the first signed
athlete to the company,

00:22:21.539 --> 00:22:25.110
and so that sneaker is
gonna fall under Judah

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:26.711
that is signed to UNITUS.

00:22:26.711 --> 00:22:29.781
And so it started there
and then it looked like,

00:22:29.781 --> 00:22:30.748
okay, what is it?

00:22:30.748 --> 00:22:32.016
- And were you there?

00:22:32.016 --> 00:22:33.685
At the factory, telling
'em this is what I want,

00:22:33.685 --> 00:22:35.219
I want this weight, I want-

00:22:35.219 --> 00:22:38.490
- I'll tell you there's a
company called SoleWorks,

00:22:38.490 --> 00:22:40.359 align:start size:84% position:16%
they're ex-Nike
guys, ex-Adidas guys

00:22:40.359 --> 00:22:41.793 align:start size:84% position:16%
that have kind of come
together and said,

00:22:41.793 --> 00:22:44.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
we wanna do one-off
shoes for certain people,

00:22:44.095 --> 00:22:47.365 align:start size:88% position:13%
so they're doing
Marshawn Lynch's cleat,

00:22:47.365 --> 00:22:48.667
I think they did a
shoe for Pharrell

00:22:48.667 --> 00:22:50.135
or something like that as well.

00:22:50.135 --> 00:22:52.771
And so I got hooked up
with them and I said,

00:22:52.771 --> 00:22:55.474
I don't know anything about
this field or this industry,

00:22:55.474 --> 00:22:57.042
and they did, so we
kind of linked up,

00:22:57.042 --> 00:22:59.177
and were able to come into
some type of partnership,

00:22:59.177 --> 00:23:01.746
and the shoe's being
made out of Vietnam.

00:23:01.746 --> 00:23:03.715
And so they've been
going back and forth,

00:23:03.715 --> 00:23:05.283 align:start size:81% position:19%
and sending me
videos and photos,

00:23:05.283 --> 00:23:07.719 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the design
process took forever.

00:23:07.719 --> 00:23:10.955
But it took pretty much
an entire year to be able

00:23:10.955 --> 00:23:12.958 align:start size:97% position:3%
to get a, this is what we
wanted the shoe to look like,

00:23:12.958 --> 00:23:15.126 align:start size:84% position:16%
this is what we
wanted to feel like,

00:23:15.126 --> 00:23:17.362 align:start position:0%
to have the prototypes, all
that stuff, and now we're here.

00:23:17.362 --> 00:23:18.829
- Right, right.

00:23:18.829 --> 00:23:21.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you involved in making
sure that the process

00:23:21.232 --> 00:23:23.034 align:start size:84% position:16%
being made in Vietnam,
all that stuff,

00:23:23.034 --> 00:23:24.502 align:start size:84% position:16%
obviously Nike
gets a lot of flack

00:23:24.502 --> 00:23:26.971 align:start size:97% position:3%
for some of their practices,
how involved are you

00:23:26.971 --> 00:23:28.373 align:start size:84% position:16%
in that kind of thing?
- 1,000%.

00:23:28.373 --> 00:23:30.275 align:start size:97% position:3%
They've assured me, they've
gone back and forth,

00:23:30.275 --> 00:23:31.909 align:start size:84% position:16%
that this is an
upstanding factory,

00:23:31.909 --> 00:23:36.080
I was very adamant about
not desiring to manufacture

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:39.050
in China and trying to
find sourcing otherwise.

00:23:39.050 --> 00:23:41.486
And we were able to, so
I'm happy about that.

00:23:41.486 --> 00:23:42.820
- That must have been complex.

00:23:42.820 --> 00:23:44.356 align:start size:97% position:3%
'Cause I feel like
everything's made out of China

00:23:44.356 --> 00:23:45.590 align:start size:84% position:16%
these days.
- Everything is made

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.091
out of China, but for
clothing and stuff,

00:23:47.091 --> 00:23:48.826 align:start size:84% position:16%
there's great
factories in Turkey,

00:23:48.826 --> 00:23:50.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a lot of the
embroidering and stitching

00:23:50.962 --> 00:23:52.197
is done right here in America.

00:23:52.197 --> 00:23:54.633
- Yeah, okay, so you
launch with the shoe,

00:23:54.633 --> 00:23:57.969
and then over the fall then
a bunch of the other products

00:23:57.969 --> 00:23:59.337 align:start size:84% position:16%
will come out?
- So on August 1st,

00:23:59.337 --> 00:24:01.740
people will be able
to buy leisure wear.

00:24:01.740 --> 00:24:05.443 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so that's gonna be
t-shirts, hoodies, sweatpants,

00:24:05.443 --> 00:24:06.811
jackets, stuff like that.

00:24:06.811 --> 00:24:08.246
And then as we move
through the fall,

00:24:08.246 --> 00:24:11.616 align:start size:97% position:3%
there's gonna be a sportswear
drop for men and women.

00:24:11.616 --> 00:24:13.251 align:start size:88% position:13%
There's also kids that's
gonna be available

00:24:13.251 --> 00:24:14.585
in the leisure wear as well.

00:24:14.585 --> 00:24:16.287 align:start size:84% position:16%
And as we get closer
to the season,

00:24:16.287 --> 00:24:17.755
we'll drop the sneaker.

00:24:17.755 --> 00:24:19.858 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then the hope is that
we'll be able to build on this

00:24:19.858 --> 00:24:22.694
and training shoes, running
shoes, walk around shoes,

00:24:22.694 --> 00:24:25.196 align:start size:97% position:3%
everything like that, and
kind of off into the sunset.

00:24:25.196 --> 00:24:28.265 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Do you view your
basketball career in some way

00:24:28.265 --> 00:24:32.103
as just the vehicle that
then became the thing to do

00:24:32.103 --> 00:24:33.505
all of this other stuff?

00:24:33.505 --> 00:24:36.007
I mean, not only the company,

00:24:36.007 --> 00:24:38.343
but the spiritual stuff
and everything else?

00:24:38.343 --> 00:24:40.244
- I would say to a degree.

00:24:40.244 --> 00:24:42.013
I love basketball.

00:24:42.013 --> 00:24:43.215
I love playing it.

00:24:43.215 --> 00:24:45.516
I loved the game ever
since I was a kid,

00:24:45.516 --> 00:24:50.589
but it has become what
I do and not who I am.

00:24:51.990 --> 00:24:53.558
I found my identity in Christ
and I just try my best to use

00:24:53.558 --> 00:24:55.760
that as a platform for who I am.

00:24:55.760 --> 00:24:58.497 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I love the game, I can't
wait to get back to it.

00:24:59.631 --> 00:25:01.433
I'm getting ready to
have a great season,

00:25:01.433 --> 00:25:02.967
I'm looking forward to it.

00:25:02.967 --> 00:25:06.771
But again, I try to use it as
a vehicle to portray who I am

00:25:06.771 --> 00:25:10.475 align:start position:0%
as an individual over basketball
being the end-all be-all

00:25:10.475 --> 00:25:12.076
to Jonathan Isaac.

00:25:12.076 --> 00:25:15.046
- Do you get any pushback
on the controversial stuff

00:25:15.046 --> 00:25:15.981
any more?
- Do I?

00:25:15.981 --> 00:25:17.381
'Cause sometimes I find people

00:25:17.381 --> 00:25:18.583
after you've been
through it enough,

00:25:18.583 --> 00:25:20.151
and you've hit big ones, right?

00:25:20.151 --> 00:25:22.754
Covid, flag, America,

00:25:22.754 --> 00:25:24.990
you've hit not just
minor ones, big ones,

00:25:24.990 --> 00:25:26.591
but sometimes you get
to the other side,

00:25:26.591 --> 00:25:28.193 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then there's a
certain type of person

00:25:28.193 --> 00:25:29.827
just completely moves on,

00:25:29.827 --> 00:25:31.696
and another type of
person kind of stays

00:25:31.696 --> 00:25:34.665
in that craziness for a while.

00:25:34.665 --> 00:25:36.668 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, I definitely
still get it.

00:25:36.668 --> 00:25:39.771 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think that my skin
has gotten a bit thicker

00:25:40.872 --> 00:25:43.908 align:start size:84% position:16%
where it's just like,
I know who I am,

00:25:43.908 --> 00:25:46.545
and I'm gonna let
you know who I am

00:25:46.545 --> 00:25:47.812 align:start size:81% position:19%
and what it is
that I believe in,

00:25:47.812 --> 00:25:49.414
and you're free to
like that or not.

00:25:49.414 --> 00:25:51.549 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I'm gonna be
authentic to myself.

00:25:51.549 --> 00:25:53.718
And so I definitely
still get pushback.

00:25:53.718 --> 00:25:55.620 align:start size:84% position:16%
I definitely I can't
tweet something

00:25:55.620 --> 00:25:56.454
without getting a tweet back

00:25:56.454 --> 00:25:57.956
(Dave laughing)

00:25:57.956 --> 00:26:00.391
about what somebody thinks
about me, which is fine.

00:26:00.391 --> 00:26:03.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
But yeah, definitely
going through the course,

00:26:03.962 --> 00:26:05.296 align:start size:84% position:16%
and kind of going
through the wringer of

00:26:05.296 --> 00:26:06.798
what does it look
like to be attacked

00:26:06.798 --> 00:26:08.232
and have your name kind of
dragged through the mud,

00:26:08.232 --> 00:26:11.836 align:start position:0%
and it does make you a
stronger, more resilient person.

00:26:11.836 --> 00:26:13.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, I'm just thinking
of this on the fly,

00:26:13.338 --> 00:26:16.741
but another guy who has said
a lot of controversial things,

00:26:16.741 --> 00:26:19.444 align:start size:97% position:3%
